  "notes": "An ichidan verb formed from {義務|ぎむ} (obligation, duty) + {付|づ}ける (to attach). Creates the meaning of attaching an obligation to something or someone. Very frequently used in passive form ({義務付|ぎむづ}けられている) to describe existing requirements.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive — takes を to mark the action being made mandatory, and に to mark who is obligated.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {義務付|ぎむづ}けられている — is required, is mandatory\n- {法律|ほうりつ}で{義務付|ぎむづ}ける — to require by law\n- {義務付|ぎむづ}けられた{研修|けんしゅう} — mandatory training\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {義務化|ぎむか}する — to make obligatory (noun + する form)\n- {強制|きょうせい}する — to compel, to force (stronger, more coercive)\n- {課|か}す — to impose (a duty, tax, etc.)",
